  <text xml:lang="ta" type="edition">
    <body>

        <div xml:id="AN216.1-kilavi">
          <p type="edition">talaimakaṭkup pāṅkāyiṉār kēṭpat taṉakkup pāṅkāyiṉārkkup parattai colliyatu.</p>
          <p type="translation" xml:lang="en">What the rival woman said to those near to herself so that those near to HER would hear.</p>
        </div>
        <div rend="parallel">
      <lg xml:id="AN216.1">
        <l>ñā<supplied>ṇ</supplied>koṇuṇ <supplied>kō</supplied>liṉ mīṉkoḷ pāṇmaka</l>
        <l>ḷakaṉpula ṉaṭaikaraip paṭutta vāra<anchor n="1"/></l>
        <l>ṉārari naṟavuṇ ṭirunta tantaikku</l>
        <l>vañci viṟakiṟ cuṭṭuvā yuṟukkun</l>
        <l>taṇṭuṟai yūraṉ peṇṭi remmaip</l>
        <l>peṭṭāṅku moḻipa <supplied>veṉpa</supplied> vavvalar</l>
        <l>paṭṭaṉa māyi ṉiṉiyeva ṉākiyar</l>
        <l>kaṭalāṭu makaḷir koyta ñāḻaluṅ</l>
        <l>kaḻaṉi yuḻavar kuṟṟa kuvaḷaiyuṅ</l>
        <l>kaṭimiḷaip puṟaviṟ pūtta mullaiyoṭu</l>
        <l>palliḷaṅ kōcar kaṇṇi yayaru </l>
        <l>mallal yāṇarc celvak kōmā</l>
        <l>ṉeṟiviṭat tulaiyāc ceṟicurai veḷvē</l>
        <l>lātaya ṉeḻiṉi yaruniṟat taḻuttiya</l>
        <l>perukaḷiṟ ṟevvam pōla</l>
        <l>varuntupu<anchor n="2"/> mātavar cēriyāñ celiṉē.</l>
      </lg>
      <lg type="translation" xml:lang="en">
        <l corresp="5ab">The man from a village by the cool ghat,</l>
        <l corresp="1">where the daughter of the bards who take fish with a fine rod with a line</l>
        <l>roasts, with Mahua as firewood, the Āral fish that was brought up</l>
        <l corresp="2+4">on the setting shore near the wide field [and] puts [it] into the mouth</l>
        <l corresp="3">of [her] father who sits there drinking toddy filtered by fibres,</l>
        <l rend="indent7">his women talk</l>
        <l corresp="5cd-6">as they like about us, they say. That gossip,</l>
        <l>if we have suffered [it], what shall happen now,</l>
        <l corresp="16a">if, suffering</l>
        <l corresp="15">as if from the trouble [caused] by the big elephant bull</l>
        <l corresp="14">that pressed [its tusk] into the precious vital spot of Ātayaṉ Eḻiṉi</l>
        <l corresp="13">with a white spear with a tight ferrule that was not ruined from throwing</l>
        <l corresp="12">[it] at the wealthy king [whose land is] very fertile,</l>
        <l corresp="11">where many young Kōcars were engaged in [making] chaplets</l>
        <l corresp="8">of Cassia plucked by the women playing by the sea,</l>
        <l corresp="9">blue waterlilies cut off by the ploughmen in the paddy fields</l>
        <l corresp="10">and jasmine flowering in the woodland in protected arbours,</l>
        <l rend="indent3" corresp="16b-d">we will go to the quarter of the beautiful man?</l>
      </lg>
        </div>
    </body>
  </text>

